Subject: [PATCH] Use injected class names in constructor and destructor declarations

GCC 16.2.1 diagnoses these template-id constructor/destructor declarations
with -Werror=template-id-cdtor in the actual C++17 build. Use the injected
class name; template parameters, specialization, bases and bodies remain
unchanged. This is also the syntax required by C++20 DR 2237.
Reference: https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/C_002b_002b-Dialect-Options.html

Regression: check-compatibility.py compiles the actual affected translation
units with their generated release flags. Original units fail in the retained
September 7 diagnostic build. No warning option is changed.

--- a/src/vpux_compiler/src/dialect/IE/transforms/passes/adapt_shapes_for_scale_shift.cpp
+++ b/src/vpux_compiler/src/dialect/IE/transforms/passes/adapt_shapes_for_scale_shift.cpp
@@ -36,8 +36,7 @@
 template <typename EltwiseOp>
 class BroadcastEltwiseRewriter final : public mlir::OpRewritePattern<EltwiseOp> {
 public:
-    BroadcastEltwiseRewriter<EltwiseOp>(mlir::MLIRContext* ctx, Logger log)
-            : mlir::OpRewritePattern<EltwiseOp>(ctx), _log(log) {
+    BroadcastEltwiseRewriter(mlir::MLIRContext* ctx, Logger log): mlir::OpRewritePattern<EltwiseOp>(ctx), _log(log) {
         this->setDebugName("BroadcastEltwiseRewriter");
     }
 
@@ -205,8 +204,7 @@
